  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the strongest configuration so far (0.650 acc, 0.628 F1), a large jump over singleprofile scvi_n200 (0.520). Aggregation (avgpool vs transformer) shows negligible difference (~0.003). The encoder effect is moderate: scvi_n200 beat pca_n2000 by ~3.5 points in singleprofile. However, scgpt—a fundamentally different pre-trained single-cell model—has not been tested at all. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 in the multiprofile setting, or is scvi_n200 the ceiling for RNA encoders? config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating the encoder effect in the highest-performing regime. Why this is the best next step: It directly tests whether a different encoder architecture can push beyond the current 0.65 ceiling, using the same profile and aggregation as our best result. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200, we gain a new direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 is the best encoder and can redirect budget toward multimodal fusion or other dimensions with greater confidence."
}

